      "notes": "Weights and rated capacity from Redington's spec chart (as hosted by Reds Fly Shop) and Trident; rated line (WF6/8/10/12/14) and spool widths (2.6/3.3/3.7/4.0/4.3 cm) from Rudi Heger's table. Diameters 3.7/4.1/4.5/4.8/5.0 in per Trident (Rudi Heger: 9.4/10.4/11.4/12.1/12.7 cm). Spool (capacity) diameters are estimates (rim − 0.24). Trident lists the 9/10/11 at \"275/300\", a typo for 275/30. The 14+ is rated with 750 yd of 50 lb GSP, entered as 30 lb (its nearest allowed value; GSP is thinner, so the solved arbor runs small). Limited Bonefish (7/8/9) and Tarpon (9/10/11) graphic editions not listed as colors. The 14+ is left out: Redington rates it with 750 yd of 50 lb GSP braid, which the backing model (20/30 lb Dacron) can't represent, and line weights stop at 12.",
